---
# Enforces this project's static-analysis policy: RAII/pointer discipline (cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory/pro-type-*), the ~60-line "one function, one screen" rule (readability-function-size), and general bug-pattern detection (bugprone-*). Vendored sources are exempted twice: their translation units via the `vendored_cgltf`/`vendored_imgui` OBJECT libraries, which never set CXX_CLANG_TIDY (target-level-only in CMake, so there is no per-source override), and their headers via ExcludeHeaderFilterRegex below.
#
# Three checks are disabled below as pure false-positive noise for this codebase's conventions, not because the underlying concern is invalid elsewhere: cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-union-access fires on glm's internal union-based vec/mat component access (.x/.y/.z), which is ordinary, well-tested library usage, not a real union-safety hazard; cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg fires on every ImGui::Text/TextColored call, ImGui's whole rendering API being printf-style vararg; and bugprone-exception-escape flags main() itself simply for calling anything that isn't noexcept (std::string/std::vector allocation, etc.) -- true of nearly every C++ program's main(), not a specific defect.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-const-cast,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-cstyle-cast,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-static-cast-downcast,
  misc-*,
  readability-function-size,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-exception-escape,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-union-access,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -misc-include-cleaner
WarningsAsErrors: ''
# clang-tidy matches with llvm::Regex (POSIX ERE), which has no lookahead: the previous '^(?!.*third_party)' form matched nothing and left every header unchecked. Exclusion needs its own key, which requires clang-tidy >= 19.
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/(include|src)/.*'
ExcludeHeaderFilterRegex: '.*third_party.*'
CheckOptions:
  - key: readability-function-size.LineThreshold
    value: '60'
  - key: readability-function-size.StatementThreshold
    value: '-1'
